--
-- Basic implementation of marching cubes mesh generation, which can be applied to an arbitrary
-- implicit function (any object with :Value(Vector3d); the optional :ValueXYZ(x, y, z) fast path is used
-- when present, see Implicit3d.luau).
--
-- Usage:
--   local mc = MarchingCubes.new()
--   mc.Implicit = Implicit3d.ImplicitSphere3d.new({ Origin = Vector3d.Zero, Radius = 1 })
--   mc.Bounds = mc.Implicit:Bounds(); mc.Bounds:Expand(0.1)
--   mc.CubeSize = 0.05
--   mc:Generate()
--   local mesh = mc.Mesh
--
-- Luau port notes:
--   * RootfindingModes enum: MarchingCubes.RootfindingModes.SingleLerp / LerpSteps / Bisection (0/1/2)
--   * ParallelCompute = true runs the same z-slab structure as C# generate_parallel, sequentially
--     (gParallel); the output is identical to ParallelCompute = false.
--   * CancelF is a plain function returning true to abort; it is polled once per x-row of cells
--     (in Roblox it can also yield, see ProgressCancel.luau).
--   * Vertex sharing: C# keeps a Dictionary<Vector3d,int> keyed on exact vertex position. Tables are keyed
--     by identity in Luau, so this port caches vertices per grid edge instead:
--       VertexHash[3 * (cx + (nx+1) * (cy + (ny+1) * cz)) + axis] = vid
--     where (cx, cy, cz) is the lower corner (in cell-corner coordinates) of the grid edge and axis is
--     0/1/2 for x/y/z. Because C# computes the crossing point of a given grid edge deterministically
--     (corner positions are computed from integer indices, root finding orders endpoints by value), both
--     schemes merge exactly the same vertices, appended in the same order. As a bonus, root finding is
--     only done once per edge (the C# version repeats it in every cell sharing the edge).
--   * The inner loops are allocation-free: corner positions/values live in reused scalar arrays.

